yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n      <frame id=\"6:103\" name=\"Fixed vs yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"241\">\n        <frame id=\"6:104\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"221\">\n          <text id=\"6:105\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"6:106\" name=\"• Frame list and exact names • Must-include content per frame (what, not how) • Navigation structure and links • All data and copy • Brand colors #4B164C + #DD88CF and Inter • Media: portraits, posts, profile grids, logo, icons • Default Button, platform shell\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"140\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"6:107\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"668\" y=\"0\" width=\"644\" height=\"241\">\n          <text id=\"6:108\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"24\" width=\"197\" height=\"23\" />\n          <text id=\"6:109\" name=\"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, backgrounds / surfaces (tints, gradients), overlays on photos, online / active, like, error / disabled • Type scale, spacing, radii, blur, elevation • All states: current tab, current profile tab, pressed, followed / liked, disabled • Headers, tab bar, tabs, story avatars, feed post, swipe card stack, action buttons, profile header, media grid, short-video overlay, sign-in sheet, drawer and menu rows • How photos are cropped and treated\" x=\"24\" y=\"57\" width=\"596\" height=\"160\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"6:110\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"64\" y=\"3468\" width=\"1312\" height=\"281\">\n      <text id=\"6:111\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"222\" height=\"35\" />\n      <text id=\"6:112\" name=\"Your file is compared with this brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any original.\" x=\"0\" y=\"51\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n      <text id=\"6:113\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current tab, current profile tab, top card of the stack, sheet / drawer presentation)\" x=\"0\" y=\"89\" width=\"1312\" height=\"154\" />\n      <text id=\"6:114\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 8 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"259\" width=\"1312\" height=\"22\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design."}],"_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"ab361835-4192-4461-a0c0-dfb4a9013d44"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01nCBoU7Yl9Wg5TClbX4UOpe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
